<!--
  The three pages of the public site, since api.html was added: the homepage, a single scroll
  page carrying the live chain reads, the hive and how it works; /disclaimers, which carries the
  deployment record and the claims register; and /api, the agent-developer page documenting the
  metered read. The seven pages that used to sit between the first two, how-it-works, agents,
  who-its-for, operators, faq, vision and status, are not listed here because they are now 301
  redirects (see _redirects), and a sitemap that lists a redirect is reported by Search Console as
  an error against the sitemap, exactly the failure this file has always avoided for the
  extension-less form below.

  The URLs are extension-less because that is what Cloudflare Pages serves as canonical: it
  redirects /disclaimers.html to /disclaimers and /index.html to /. Listing the .html forms would
  make every entry in this file a redirect, which is the same Search Console error described above.

  No <lastmod>, <changefreq> or <priority>. Search engines ignore the latter two outright, and a
  <lastmod> that is not updated with the page is a worse signal than none at all.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url><loc>https://rwally.com/</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://rwally.com/disclaimers</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://rwally.com/api</loc></url>
</urlset>
